=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play status/lockout ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's main menu, its header, risk level and$
# status rows read by the real checks, header probe and risk$
# level from a simulated host, hostfake's host.System, whose$
# commands a model of the host answers. Its items lead to the$
# screen mocks, which show Figma's host, not this one, on the$
# gallery's fixture plans. Nothing on this machine changes.$
$
# Info: status/lockout$
# The hardened host, but ufw allows 443 alone, so it refuses SSH$
# on 2230: a new SSH session cannot log in.$
$
hardn  v0.4.0              https://github.com/abbott/hardn$
$
# Debian 13 (Trixie) ###########################################$
$
  [web-01]                 192.0.2.20$
                           3 days, 5 hours, 12 minutes$
$
  [*] Risk Level           Critical ~ lockout risk$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
  [*] Firewall             Partial ssh blocked$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [+] SSH Port             Configured non-default (2230)$
  [+] AppArmor             Configured 7 profiles enforced$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured unattended-upgrades$
$
----------------------------------------------------------------$
$
  Select an option         Dry-run Mode Disabled$
$
   1) User Management      Create, Configure (sudo, SSH keys)$
   2) SSH Login            Toggle SSH root access$
   3) DNS                  Configure Nameservers$
   4) Firewall             Configure UFW rules$
   5) Backup               Configure Hardn backup settings$
   6) Dry-Run              Simulate changes$
   7) Run All              Execute hardening operations$
   8) Environment          Configure environment variable$
   9) System Details       View system information$
  10) Logs                 View log file$
$
   0) Exit                 q to quit$
$
  > Enter selection [0-10 or q]: q$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

